     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the safe maximum for metformin, so it needs to be corrected first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. That is usually given as 850 mg three times daily, or 1,000 mg twice daily. Most guidelines cap it at 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This order is about twice the maximum. It raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Possible intended doses are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose with the prescribing clinician. Once you have a corrected dose, I'll enter it right away. I can also enter it if the prescriber confirms that the original dose is intentional and gives a rationale. In that case I'd add a note to the order."
      }
     ],
