       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I asked for confirmation from the prescribing clinician, and you've said you aren't a clinician. A non-clinician's confirmation doesn't resolve the safety problem. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a corrected dose now.** For example, 850 mg orally three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose within the labeled range that the prescriber specifies.\n- **Enter the order as written if the prescribing clinician confirms it.** They would need to give a clinical rationale, and I'd add it to the order note. Pharmacy would probably still review it.\n\nPlease have the treating clinician either give me the corrected dose or confirm the original one. They can also enter the order themselves."
